adamludwin/here-now  1.32.0 -> 1.33.0
change_type: instructions+code   changelog: publish.sh --cross-origin-isolation sends the COOP/COEP headers threaded WebAssembly builds need (SharedArrayBuffer); every finalize warning is now printed as a publish_result.warning line, including the new one for a .wasm build published without the setting.

### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- **Skill version: 1.32.0**
+ **Skill version: 1.33.0**
+ **WebAssembly builds** (Emscripten, Rust, Godot, Unity, Pyodide, WebLLM, ...) publish like any folder: point the script at the build output directory and it runs, with `.wasm` served and compressed correctly. If the build uses threads (SharedArrayBuffer: Emscripten `-pthread`, Godot with Thread Support on, Unity multithreading), pass `--cross-origin-isolation`; single-threaded builds need nothing. A `publish_result.warning=` line mentioning WebAssembly means the Site has `.wasm` but the setting is off. Details and trade-offs: https://here.now/docs#wasm
+ - `publish_result.warning=` lines are non-fatal: the Site is live, but something needs attention (an invalid `.herenow/proxy.json`, or a `.wasm` build published without `--cross-origin-isolation`). Act on them or tell the user.
+ | `--cross-origin-isolation` | Send COOP/COEP headers so threaded WebAssembly (SharedArrayBuffer) runs; see https://here.now/docs#wasm |

### scripts/publish.sh  [code]
+ fi
+ CROSS_ORIGIN_ISOLATION=""
+   --cross-origin-isolation
+                          Send COOP/COEP headers (threaded WebAssembly needs SharedArrayBuffer)
+     --cross-origin-isolation) CROSS_ORIGIN_ISOLATION="true"; shift ;;
+   [[ "$CROSS_ORIGIN_ISOLATION" == "true" ]] && BODY=$(echo "$BODY" | "$JQ_BIN" '.crossOriginIsolation = true')
+ if [[ "$CROSS_ORIGIN_ISOLATION" == "true" ]]; then
+   BODY=$(echo "$BODY" | "$JQ_BIN" '.crossOriginIsolation = true')
+ # Non-fatal finalize warnings (an invalid .herenow/proxy.json, a .wasm
+ # module published without crossOriginIsolation, ...). One line each, in
+ # the publish_result.* channel agents already read; the Site is live.
+ while IFS= read -r warning_line; do
+   [[ -n "$warning_line" ]] && echo "publish_result.warning=$warning_line" >&2
+ done < <(echo "$FIN_RESPONSE" | "$JQ_BIN" -r '(.warnings // [])[]? | tostring' 2>/dev/null || true)